vermintide - occupies a unique part of  the game space it's based on a franchise  that historically has been a little  inaccessible and real nerdy in all the  best ways but his basic moment-to-moment  gameplay is accessible to anyone with  thumbs and a compunction to smash waves  of enemies on top of that it's deep  enough to keep the truly dedicated happy  you know the ones that list min maxing  might dwarf slayer as an interest in  their dating profiles hit me up if  you're out there at the heart of it it's  also something very familiar it's very  difficult to describe vermintide without  leaning on similarities - left for dead  fundamentally they're both games about  holding off hordes of foul enemies while  frantically scrambling for safety they  use special enemies to throw wrenches  into the best-laid plans of you and your  three allies and by the end of each  session you'll be a mixture of elated  and terrified their DNA is very similar  but vermin tied to just became the  mutated rat-faced cousin of valve zombie  shooter and it's precisely that reason  that I love it so much  before anyone says yeah obviously Dave  loves it he's a GameSpot Warhammer nerd  I I can't disagree with you I am that  but I adore this game despite the rabbit  Warhammer fandom it's fun regardless of  whether you love Warhammer or not and  either way I prefer 40k anyway but while  the core of vermintide taps into the  nearly decade old left 4 dead 2 even  down to the starting camera angles and  chatter between characters the amount of  new features and wrinkles it brings the  genre outweigh the number of  inspirations it took now I put a huge  amount of time into leopard a2 but it  was always umber Steven despite the best  efforts of the game's AI director I'd  become fatigued by the sameness I craved  some more variety something different to  challenge me each time and there was  only so many times we could carry noam  chomsky 3 around I kept coming back for  that rad guitar riff a victory but over  time it started to feel a little bit  less enticing the AI director's job was  to try and keep each round feeling new  and different by placing enemies in  response to your behavior this would on  paper keep you on the edge of your seat  and punish you for your mistakes women  tied to aims to do something similar but  its director has studied valves and set  out to pick up where it left off with so  many hours in left 4 dead 2 it would get  to the point where players wouldn't know  where to expect tanks and what strategy  works best against the giant beasts but  vermintide too has gone to extra lengths  to ensure you never become comfortable  and it never becomes predictable it will  try to separate you with gas bombs or  ambush loan players with gutter honors  you could run through part of level once  and never see a single storm fiend and  then the next time a huge lumbering  Beast could pinch you in a corner and  immolate you with warp fire that truly  is nowhere safe which makes a  hard-fought victory all the more sweeter  if you explore the levels which in  itself is a challenge because the longer  you linger the more chance there is of a  hook rats snatching you away you can  find tomes and grimoires each of which  increase the value of the loot you win  at the end of a run but tomes take up a  valuable healing slot and grimoires can  massively reduce your maximum HP but as  much as the game is already challenging  you you'll want that extra struggle  because it's so much fun to earn a new  set of pistols that really finish off  your witch hunter build creating an  element of risk and reward with  in each match and tying it to new  equipment and character progression  makes repeat players feel fresh there's  so many more variables for you to think  about and for the AI director to  manipulate which also means women tied  to becomes an experience with longevity  it's obvious to say but the additional  varied classes with their own suite of  perks and abilities brings a ton of  replayability to a game - which is  important when you consider that  vermintide revolves around surviving  increasingly challenging levels  repeatedly the game taps into warhammers  deep source material to create  characters that are interesting to fans  while also keeping them accessible  enough so that anyone can identify and  enjoy them you can easily slip into your  tank rogue fighter or Ranger character  with a little experimentation while it  was fun mowing down zombies with an  assault rifle standing side by side to a  dwarf that's wielding a shield half the  size of him while a fire mage slings  balls of flame over your shoulder adds a  certain cinematic thrill to the action  and since builds change that moment of  going back to back where the teammate  never become stale in game there's  always someone different by your side  even when the person controlling them is  the same and you'll have a lot of these  moments obviously one of the biggest  changes between left of dead and  vermintide is the focus on melee combat  but it's way deeper and more nuanced  than I'd expected sure it's easy to  glance at a gameplay video and think yet  this is left-click o'clock and spamming  attacks is the order of the day but  there's much more to consider when it  comes to your character in your arsenal  and it's these elements that give you  options in the middle of a tough  skirmish have you got daggers you'll be  attacking nice and fast but you should  go for crits and your block will be  pretty weak using a hammer you'll have  big wide sweeps that are good for crowd  control but you're slow attacks might  hamper you against the big special  enemies wielding a flail you can go  around shields but make sure that it's  your job to focus shield using enemies  vermintide - makes you feel like you're  constantly on the edge of being  overwhelmed but in those moments when  everything clicks and you're pushing  back waves and waves of enemies axes  cleaving through rats fireballs and  arrows flying through the skies and  you're left on a slither of health  surrounded by your defeated foes you  feel like a goddamn hero  and that's not a feeling that is easy to  stir in a player so frequently yeah at  the end of a difficult vermintide run as  you step through that portal to victory  you breathe a sigh of heavy relief and  start thinking about venturing back in  all over again  so that's my take on vermintide - coming  from a guy who's played a heck of a lot  left 4 dead 2 it stood so many similar  emotions in me but it's also created  something so new and unique and it's  been amazing to see people enjoy it so  far especially as it's a Warhammer game  I was already invested in the fandom if  you've been enjoying vermintide - let me  know in the comments section below if  you've got a different opinion on the  argument the vermintide - picks up where  left4dead left off then be sure to shout  at me in the comment section below as  well and make sure you stick around and  I promise I will talk about a game that  isn't focused on a Warhammer universe  soon thanks for watching and I'll see  you in the next one
 

